{"comment_text": {"ja61:0.1": "", "ja61:0.2": "", "ja61:0.3": "", "ja61:0.4": "", "ja61:1.1": "A young student is told by his mother that his education is incomplete until he learns the mysterious “spell of the unpleasant”. His teacher knows that there is no such spell, but realizes that the mother wants her son to learn of the wickedness of women. | Read <i lang='pi' translate='no'>asā</i> from <i lang='pi' translate='no'>a</i> + <i lang='pi' translate='no'>sva</i>, “without an owner”, and hence “unclaimed” or “without a husband”. The commentary explains, rather, as <i lang='pi' translate='no'>asatiyo</i> (“false”) and also <i lang='pi' translate='no'>asāta</i> (“displeasing”). Perhaps the curious “spell of the unpleasant” was retroactively invented to explain this word. ", "ja61:1.2": "", "ja61:1.3": "", "ja61:1.4": "", "ja61:1.5": "", "ja61:1.6": "", "ja61:2.1": ""}, "html_text": {"ja61:0.1": "<article id='ja61'><header><ul><li class='division'>{}</li>", "ja61:0.2": "<li>{}</li>", "ja61:0.3": "<li>{}</li></ul>", "ja61:0.4": "<h1 class='sutta-title'>{}</h1></header>", "ja61:1.1": "<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja61:1.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja61:1.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja61:1.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja61:1.5": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja61:1.6": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p></blockquote>", "ja61:2.1": "<p class='endsutta'>{}</p></article>"}, "root_text": {"ja61:0.1": "Jātaka ", "ja61:0.2": "Ekakanipāta ", "ja61:0.3": "Itthivagga ", "ja61:0.4": "1. Asātamantajātaka ", "ja61:1.1": "“Asā lokitthiyo nāma, ", "ja61:1.2": "velā tāsaṁ na vijjati; ", "ja61:1.3": "Sārattā ca pagabbhā ca, ", "ja61:1.4": "sikhī sabbaghaso yathā; ", "ja61:1.5": "Tā hitvā pabbajissāmi, ", "ja61:1.6": "vivekamanubrūhayan”ti. ", "ja61:2.1": "Asātamantajātakaṁ paṭhamaṁ. "}, "translation_text": {"ja61:0.1": "Stories of Past Lives 61 ", "ja61:0.2": "The Book of the Ones ", "ja61:0.3": "Women ", "ja61:0.4": "The Spell of the Unpleasant: a past life story ", "ja61:1.1": "The women in the world called unclaimed—", "ja61:1.2": "there is no confining them. ", "ja61:1.3": "They are rude and full of desires, ", "ja61:1.4": "like an all-consuming flame. ", "ja61:1.5": "Leaving them behind, I shall go forth ", "ja61:1.6": "and foster seclusion. ", "ja61:2.1": ""}, "reference_text": {"ja61:0.1": "", "ja61:0.2": "", "ja61:0.3": "", "ja61:0.4": "", "ja61:1.1": "bj30.26, dr27.21, ms22J_135, msdiv61, ndp22.16, pts-vp-pli1.288", "ja61:1.2": "", "ja61:1.3": "", "ja61:1.4": "", "ja61:1.5": "", "ja61:1.6": "", "ja61:2.1": "ms22J_136"}, "keys_order": ["ja61:0.1", "ja61:0.2", "ja61:0.3", "ja61:0.4", "ja61:1.1", "ja61:1.2", "ja61:1.3", "ja61:1.4", "ja61:1.5", "ja61:1.6", "ja61:2.1"]}